window.GLOSS={};
window.EN={"1":"Having taken Thracia Castle, Celice pressed on, marching straight for Grannvale.","2":"What Celice and his companions found upon reaching Miletos, south of the Empire,","3":"was the sight of a cluster of cities that had once built immense wealth through trade, free from any one power's rule,","4":"now dying out under the combined rule of the Empire and the dark cult.","5":"Queen Hilda of Kronos Castle,","6":"with a cruelty that seemed almost like madness, drove countless citizens to their deaths,","7":"while Archbishop Manfroy of Miletos Castle ordered Bishop Morgan of Rados Castle","8":"to carry out a merciless hunt for children.","9":"Wealth, freedom, hope, even life itself — all of it was being stripped from the people's hands.","10":"Celice could not stand by and watch","11":"as people were killed one after another, sacrificed to the dark cult's rituals.","12":"After a fierce battle drove off the imperial army and saved the free city of Perluke, the Liberation Army","13":"was welcomed by the citizens with cheers of joy.","14":"The hope of Miletos, which had nearly been lost, was, with the Liberation Army's arrival,","15":"finally about to draw breath once more.","16":"(Julius): Ishtar, how is the plan progressing?","17":"(Ishtar): Yes sir, steadily...","18":"(Julius): Heh... a sacrifice to the dark god. The townsfolk must be terrified.","19":"(Ishtar): There isn't a parent who wouldn't grieve, learning their own child is to be burned alive. Especially a mother's sorrow...","20":"(Julius): Hehe... good, that's exactly right. Give them despair.","21":"(Julius): People who have lost all hope of living become as docile as puppets — perfect slaves for the Loptr Empire.","22":"(Ishtar): And what shall we do with the children we've gathered? This castle is already holding more than it can fit.","23":"(Julius): Send them to the imperial capital Belhalla as they come. The children will be educated under me.","24":"(Julius): Friend or sibling, it makes no difference — I'll have them hate and kill each other.","25":"(Julius): Only those who survive will become the Empire's new subjects, loyal servants of Loptous.","26":"(Ishtar): But Lord Julius, what about Emperor Arvis?","27":"(Ishtar): I hear the Emperor said he would never permit the child-hunting, no matter what.","28":"(Julius): Father? Hehehe... no need to worry. Leave it to me...","29":"(Ishtar): Lord Julius...","30":"(Hilda): Ishtar, where is His Highness Prince Julius?","31":"(Ishtar): Ah, mother... the prince has returned to Belhalla.","32":"(Hilda): I see... but tell me, how are things going? It seems the prince is fond of you, but will he actually make you his bride?","33":"(Ishtar): That is...","34":"(Hilda): Pull yourself together.","35":"(Hilda): Our House Friege is one of Grannvale's great noble families, and I myself am of Veltomer blood, same as the imperial family.","36":"(Hilda): There's no one more fitting than you to be the prince's match.","37":"(Ishtar): Yes...","38":"(Hilda): In any case, Ishtar — my husband Bloom and my son Ishtore were both struck down by the rebels,","39":"(Hilda): and our territory of Alster was seized by the enemy. Celice, along with his father, is House Friege's most hated enemy.","40":"(Hilda): I will meet the rebels here at Kronos Castle myself,","41":"(Hilda): while you return to Miletos and arrange for the children we've gathered to be sent to the capital.","42":"(Ishtar): Yes, mother...","43":"(Dark Priest): Lady Hilda, the placement of the mages is complete.","44":"(Dark Priest): However, it seems some of the children fled the castle amid the confusion. What should we do?","45":"(Hilda): What did you say!? How foolish... hmph, well, never mind. Kill them all, as an example to the rest.","46":"(Hilda): Order General Rideau of Rados Castle to execute the children who escaped.","47":"(Girl): Hey, where should we run to?","48":"(Boy): I don't know that either.","49":"(Girl): But then, what are we...","50":"(Boy): Don't cry... it'll be alright. The holy warrior will save us. Believe that, okay?","51":"(Girl): Mm... you're right, the holy warrior... surely, they'll come for us... surely...","52":"(Kubly): General Rideau, orders have come from Lady Hilda of Kronos to move out.","53":"(Rideau): Is that so, how gracious of her. This kind of work isn't fit for warriors like us.","54":"(Rideau): I've had quite enough of hunting children. Do the rest as you please.","55":"(Kubly): How unfortunate for you — this time's job is apparently executing the children who escaped.","56":"(Rideau): Wh-, what did you say...","57":"(Kubly): If you're a soldier of the Empire, you have no choice but to obey orders.","58":"(Kubly): Or are you planning to betray Emperor Arvis?","59":"(Rideau): ...no... that, I cannot do. I alone will never betray His Majesty Arvis... understood... there's no helping it...","60":"(Kubly): Heh... soldiers really are foolish creatures.","61":"(Manfroy): Princess Julia, I've found you...","62":"(Julia): Eh? Who are you...?","63":"(Manfroy): Kukuku... it seems the shock even took your memories. Well, never mind — come with me.","64":"(Julia): No, please, let go of me!","65":"(Manfroy): Hehehe... resisting me is pointless. Give up.","66":"(Julia): Ahh... help... Lord Celice...","67":"(Levin (Strategist)): Celice, it seems the children have fled from Kronos. At this rate, they'll be killed.","68":"(Celice): The children!? Understood, let's set out at once. We need to save as many as we can.","69":"(Levin (Strategist)): But Celice, Julia is nowhere to be seen. I've been searching for her since a while ago, but...","70":"(Celice): Julia's gone? Why would this happen!! Don't tell me...","71":"(Levin (Strategist)): Yes. I can't think of any other explanation than that the enemy has captured her.","72":"(Levin (Strategist)): I don't know why they'd be after Julia, though...","73":"(Celice): Ngh... Julia, wait for me, I will definitely come save you!","74":"(Rideau): Well, there's no need to rush. All troops, advance at a leisurely pace...","75":"(Shanan): You've grown strong, Celice. You truly are the child of Lord Sigurd and Lady Deirdre. I can't even hold a candle to you anymore.","76":"(Celice): That's thanks to you too, Shanan.","77":"(Celice): When I was small, you were the one who taught me swordsmanship — that's how I became this strong.","78":"(Shanan): Heh... you really are something...","79":"(Celice): Shanan, you seem a little tired. I wish I could share some of my strength with you...","80":"(Shanan): Hey now, are you going to start treating me like an old man too? I'm still young, you know.","81":"(Celice): Ah, sorry, I didn't mean it that way...","82":"(Shanan): Heh, it's fine. I'll gratefully accept the thought, at least.","83":"(Leaf): Sister, what's wrong? You look a little tired.","84":"(Altena): Ah, Leaf... no, it's nothing. Don't worry about it.","85":"(Leaf): If that's the case, that's fine...","86":"(Leaf): If there's anything I can do, please, tell me anything at all. I want to be of help to you, sister.","87":"(Altena): Thank you, Leaf... actually, I was thinking about Arion.","88":"(Leaf): I thought as much... Prince Arion was carried off by someone, wasn't he?","89":"(Altena): The one who took him was Prince Julius, apparently...","90":"(Leaf): The Empire's Prince Julius!? But for what purpose?","91":"(Altena): Probably to try to win him over as an ally.","92":"(Leaf): Then, does that mean we'll have to fight the Thracian knight corps again?","93":"(Altena): Yes, if things continue this way... I can't help but feel it's such a shame...","94":"(Leaf): But sister, I think it's a good thing.","95":"(Altena): Eh... why is that?","96":"(Leaf): Because Arion wasn't dead after all — that means there's still hope, doesn't it?","97":"(Leaf): Sister, it'll be alright. Given time, everything will work out. Please, don't give up hope.","98":"(Altena): Leaf... thank you, somehow I feel a bit more cheerful now.","99":"(Leaf): I'm glad. Just seeing you look so sad is painful for me too, sister.","100":"(Leaf): I want you to be happy, sister. For that, I would do absolutely anything!","101":"(Nanna): Lord Leaf, I'd heard the towns of the Miletos region were such rich places, but to see them so utterly devastated like this...","102":"(Leaf): Yeah... I never imagined the Empire's rule here could be this terrible.","103":"(Leaf): This area is a merchant city where all sorts of goods gather,","104":"(Leaf): so in peaceful times, it must have been quite lively.","105":"(Nanna): Yes, as a child I always admired it — Miletos's beautiful streets, the rare goods sold there...","106":"(Nanna): I always thought it must be so wonderful...","107":"(Leaf): Demaggio... once this war is over, once peace returns, let's come to this city together again, the two of us.","108":"(Nanna): Eh...?","109":"(Leaf): My parents, you know, came to this city together once, and bought a lovely tiara made of pearls for my mother.","110":"(Nanna): Yes...","111":"(Leaf): So, for you too...","112":"(Nanna): Lord Leaf.........","113":"(Leaf): Haha, what am I even saying. Anyway, for now, we need to bring down the Empire as soon as possible.","114":"(Leaf): Demaggio, just a little more patience. Please, do your best!","115":"(Nanna): Yes! Lord Leaf!!","116":"(Fabal): You... such a delicate little body, and yet you're really something. Aren't you scared?","117":"(Nanna): It would be a lie to say I'm not scared. But when I think of the captured children, I just can't sit still.","118":"(Fabal): Hmm, so you like children, huh.","119":"(Nanna): Yeah, I love them.","120":"(Nanna): I hear you, Fabal, raised children who'd lost their parents — that's an admirable thing.","121":"(Fabal): It's not like that... Patty just told me to, so there was no helping it. It's not like I particularly like kids.","122":"(Nanna): Heheh, nothing but lies — I saw it myself.","123":"(Nanna): When you left the country to join the Liberation Army, all those little children clung to you, crying.","124":"(Nanna): Those children thought of you like a father.","125":"(Fabal): C-, cut it out... I just... I'm leaving now, see ya!","126":"(Nanna): Heheh, that Fabal...","127":"(Lester): Hey there, Patty — still as lively as ever, I see.","128":"(Patty): Oh, Lester. None of your business.","129":"(Lester): See, picking a fight again — that's a bad habit of yours.","130":"(Patty): You're one to talk, Lester — you're always the one teasing me.","131":"(Lester): Huh, was I?","132":"(Patty): Yes, you were — you don't even think of me as a girl, do you.","133":"(Lester): Huh? Patty's a girl?","134":"(Patty): ! ...you idiot!!","135":"(Lester): Sorry, sorry, it was a joke. Come on, don't be mad...","136":"(Lester): I, uh, think about you a lot, you know, so that's why I ended up saying that... sorry.","137":"(Patty): What do you mean, you think about me?","138":"(Lester): You're so dense! I like you, that's what I mean!!","139":"(Boy): Eh, the Liberation Army? Whoa, you really came!","140":"(Boy): Ah, it's the Liberation Army! Whoa, that's so cool!!","141":"(Boy): Eh? You're the holy warrior? Really? Huh...","142":"(Girl): Ah, the holy warrior... waah, I was so scared~","143":"(Girl): Are you with the Liberation Army? Wow~, how wonderful...","144":"(Girl): Thank you for saving us.","145":"(Rideau): It's been a while since I've had a worthy battle. My thanks for that.","146":"(Rideau): Heh... I suppose this too is fate...","147":"(Hilda): For my father, my husband, and my son's grudge... know your place!!","148":"(Hilda): Ngh... how could this be... I'd better retreat for now...","149":"(Celice): Levin, the children who were being held — where are they?","150":"(Levin (Strategist)): It seems they've already been sent to Miletos. Celice, let's hurry to liberate Miletos — the children are in danger.","151":"(Oifey): Lord Celice, once we cross the Miletos Strait, we'll be in the Chalphy Duchy.","152":"(Celice): The Chalphy Duchy... my father's homeland. You must feel nostalgic, Oifey.","153":"(Oifey): Yes, of course. I have so many memories in Chalphy.","154":"(Oifey): Lord Sigurd and Lady Ethlyn, and also Naoise and Alec and the other young knights — I often played with them.","155":"(Oifey): They were all such kind people.","156":"(Celice): Hmm... but I can't really understand it, since I've never been there even once.","157":"(Oifey): That's true. Lord Celice, you were born in Agustria, and grew up in Silesse and Isaac.","158":"(Oifey): Come to think of it, you've never once set foot in Grannvale.","159":"(Celice): Yeah, but it feels strange somehow... that I'm supposedly the prince of Grannvale... it feels like I'm deceiving everyone.","160":"(Oifey): I understand how you feel, my prince. But you should also understand the feelings of the powerless people.","161":"(Oifey): They have struggled for so long under the Empire's tyranny, and have been longing for a savior to appear.","162":"(Celice): And you're saying that savior is supposed to be me?","163":"(Oifey): Yes, the people wish for the return of the hero Sigurd,","164":"(Oifey): and they're overlaying that image onto the legendary child he's said to have had with Princess Deirdre.","165":"(Celice): The legendary child, huh... sometimes the people's fervor frightens me. They look at me with eyes as if they were looking at a god...","166":"(Oifey): That just shows how harsh the Empire's rule has been.","167":"(Oifey): For example, even here in Miletos, young children are torn from their parents, and anyone who resists meets with utter slaughter.","168":"(Oifey): This is the work of devils. It's not something humans would do.","169":"(Celice): Oifey, do you also think Emperor Arvis is the dark god Loptous?","170":"(Oifey): That's what the people seem to think, but I don't believe that.","171":"(Celice): Then, is it Manfroy who's Loptous?","172":"(Oifey): My prince... in any case, we must hurry. The dark god is surely awakening.","173":"(Oifey): If the people praise you as their holy warrior, you must answer that cry.","174":"(Kubly): Know well the terror of my dark magic!","175":"(Kubly): Archbishop Manfroy... please, forgive me...","176":"(Celice): ...it's like a ghost town.","177":"(Levin (Strategist)): The mages under Morgan's command massacred the citizens who resisted...","178":"(Celice): How could this be... it's terrible... far too terrible!","179":"(Levin (Strategist)): Celice, now you understand why we must fight.","180":"(Levin (Strategist)): Under the Empire's rule, good people cannot survive — this is the way of the Loptr Empire...","181":"(Celice): Fee, Levin says he has something to talk to you about. I'll go on ahead, so take your time talking.","182":"(Levin (Strategist)): Fee, you really are a stubborn one. In that way, you're just like Fury.","183":"(Fee): ! .........","184":"(Levin (Strategist)): Don't be so angry. It was wrong of me to ignore you. I'm sorry.","185":"(Fee): Father, you're far too cruel!! The first time I saw you, at the castle in Ribot, I doubted my own eyes.","186":"(Fee): I was so happy... the tears just wouldn't stop coming...","187":"(Fee): And yet, father, you didn't say a single word to me!","188":"(Fee): Do you have any idea how lonely that made me feel!","189":"(Levin (Strategist)): And so you pretended not to notice either, is that it?","190":"(Fee): I decided something — that I would absolutely hold out, until you spoke to me first, father...","191":"(Levin (Strategist)): Heh... you really are a troublesome one...","192":"(Fee): Hmph! ...if you're going to say things like that, I won't talk to you anymore!!","193":"(Fee): Because you're the kind of man you are, father, that's why mother Fury...","194":"(Levin (Strategist)): Fee, I know it was wrong, what happened with Fury.","195":"(Levin (Strategist)): But that's a matter between the two of us, as husband and wife. It's not something you children should speak up about!","196":"(Fee): Father!!","197":"(Levin (Strategist)): Right now, just focus on winning this battle. Understood, Fee!","198":"(Celice): Lene, Levin says he has something to talk to you about. I'll go on ahead, so take your time talking.","199":"(Levin (Strategist)): Lene, don't be too reckless out there. If that beautiful face of yours gets scarred, the men will all be in mourning.","200":"(Lene): Say, Mr. Levin, you wouldn't happen to know anything about my mother, would you?","201":"(Levin (Strategist)): Hm? Why would you think I'd know your mother?","202":"(Lene): Because Mr. Levin seems to know everything.","203":"(Levin (Strategist)): You want to know about your mother?","204":"(Lene): Yes! And about my father too.","205":"(Levin (Strategist)): Lene, you are who you are. Don't worry about your parents. But I'll teach you one thing, at least.","206":"(Levin (Strategist)): Your parents loved each other truly, with all their hearts, and that's how they came to have a child like you. There's no falsehood in that.","207":"(Levin (Strategist)): There was a sad parting, but even now, they're watching over you.","208":"(Lene): I... ever since I was small, I always felt like someone was watching over me.","209":"(Lene): Was that really my father? But if he's alive, why won't he show himself to me!","210":"(Lene): I've been waiting all this time, and it's lonely, unbearably so...","211":"(Levin (Strategist)): Lene...","212":"(Celice): Tinny, Levin says he has something to talk to you about.","213":"(Celice): I'll go on ahead, so take your time talking.","214":"(Levin (Strategist)): Tinny, Hilda was your aunt, wasn't she. Is this fight hard on you?","215":"(Tinny): No, Lady Hilda was always such a terrifying person...","216":"(Levin (Strategist)): Did she mistreat you?","217":"(Tinny): Yes, she cursed at me with foul words many times, and struck me — calling my mother a traitor...","218":"(Levin (Strategist)): Tinny's mother was Tiltyu, wasn't she...","219":"(Tinny): Yes, after the battle of Belhalla, she fled to Silesse together with brother Arthur, and there, she gave birth to me.","220":"(Tinny): My father had already passed away, I'm told...","221":"(Levin (Strategist)): I see... and after that, to the kingdom of Alster?","222":"(Tinny): Yes, King Bloom's men came to Silesse, and forcibly took us away.","223":"(Tinny): And there, mother passed away...","224":"(Levin (Strategist)): It must have been an awfully hard time for her...","225":"(Tinny): Yes... Hilda treated mother as her sworn enemy...","226":"(Tinny): Mother endured it all for my sake, but I don't think there was ever a day her tears truly dried...","227":"(Levin (Strategist)): ...I see... so that's how it was...","228":"(Tinny): Lord Levin? ...is something wrong?","229":"(Levin (Strategist)): Mm... why do you ask?","230":"(Tinny): Because, Lord Levin, your eyes...","231":"(Levin (Strategist)): Ah, this... this is just sweat, don't worry about it...","232":"(Arvis): Ishtar, it's been a while — are you well?","233":"(Ishtar): Ah, Your Majesty! Why have you come here?","234":"(Arvis): Ishtar, release the children gathered in this castle. This work can't possibly be to your own liking either.","235":"(Ishtar): But, Prince Julius's orders...","236":"(Arvis): I will speak to Julius myself. Don't worry.","237":"(Ishtar): But...","238":"(Arvis): This is an order, Ishtar. Or are you saying you cannot obey the command of your emperor?","239":"(Ishtar): No... that's not what I meant...","240":"(Julius): Father, it troubles me when you act on your own like this. Ishtar is my subordinate, you know.","241":"(Arvis): Julius! You...","242":"(Julius): Father still doesn't seem to understand. ...You're getting on in years now — wouldn't it be about time to retire?","243":"(Julius): Or is it that you're still thinking of exiling me, perhaps?","244":"(Arvis): No... I know it's pointless to defy you... I'll say no more...","245":"(Julius): Then don't go wandering around a place like this — go back to your own castle.","246":"(Julius): You have an important duty waiting for you, father — the defense of Chalphy Castle!","247":"(Arvis): Ah.........","248":"(Manfroy): Kukuku... emperor in name only... even His Majesty Arvis has become such a pitiable thing.","249":"(Julius): Manfroy. How is Julia doing? Has she recovered her memories?","250":"(Manfroy): She is held captive at Chalphy Castle, and it seems Julia has remembered everything.","251":"(Manfroy): That as a child, she was nearly killed by her own twin brother, Your Highness,","252":"(Manfroy): and that she was cast outside the castle by her mother's magic...","253":"(Julius): That's right. I disposed of Deirdre myself. Knowing she was to be killed by her own son, that woman accepted her fate quietly.","254":"(Julius): But with her very last strength, she managed to let only her daughter escape.","255":"(Julius): Julia has inherited the power of the goddess Naga from Deirdre.","256":"(Julius): She must be killed... before it's too late.","257":"(Manfroy): But the Scripture of Naga should still be sealed away in Belhalla.","258":"(Manfroy): I find it hard to believe that the goddess Naga truly dwells within Julia...","259":"(Julius): Don't make me say the same thing over and over. The avatar of Naga, the bloodline of House Heim — it must be erased from this world!","260":"(Manfroy): Understood. Then I'll order my subordinates to kill her.","261":"(Julius): Mm, don't fail this time. I must return to Belhalla.","262":"(Manfroy): Yes sir. Then this land will be defended with the full strength of our cult.","263":"(Manfroy): We'll bring down Celice, and present him before Your Highness.","264":"(Julius): Celice, huh... the people call him the Prince of Light, I hear. Heh, which would make me the Prince of Darkness, I suppose.","265":"(Julius): Both of us, children of Princess Deirdre, holding the right of succession to the Grannvale throne. The sort of story fools would love.","266":"(Manfroy): That brat must be killed. If we let him live, he'll become a great calamity.","267":"(Julius): He's only inherited the power of the holy warrior Baldr, I believe.","268":"(Julius): There's not much need to worry over that, but well, never mind — do as you like.","269":"(Manfroy): Yes sir.........","270":"(Ishtar): Lord Julius...","271":"(Julius): Ishtar, let's leave this place to the dark priests and head home.","272":"(Julius): That's right — while we're at it, why don't the two of us have some fun together? Let's offer up one traitor as a sacrifice.","273":"(Julius): A contest, to see which of us can finish him off first.","274":"(Ishtar): Yes, understood. In that case, gladly!","275":"(Julius): Fufufu... Ishtar, it seems I've won.","276":"(Julius): Playtime's over, let's go home.","277":"(Ishtar): Lord Julius, it seems I'm the one who's won.","278":"(Ishtar): Eh? Why...","279":"— (if Julius wins)","280":"(Julius): Heh, Ishtar, it seems I've won.","281":"(Ishtar): As expected of you, Lord Julius, splendidly done.","282":"— (if Ishtar wins)","283":"(Ishtar): Heheh, Lord Julius, it seems I'm the one who's won.","284":"(Julius): Heh... Ishtar, not bad at all.","285":"— (if Ishtar loses)","286":"(Julius): You've lost, it seems. Come now, let's go home!","287":"— (if Miletos Castle is captured without defeating either of them)","288":"(Julius): Playtime's over, let's go home, Ishtar.","289":"(Ishtar): Yes, Lord Julius.","290":"(Zagam): Hehehe... curse your own misfortune...","291":"(Zagam): Archbishop Manfroy, please, forgive me...","292":"(Levin (Strategist)): Celice, it seems we were too late. The children appear to have been taken away to Grannvale.","293":"(Celice): How could this... ngh...","294":"(Levin (Strategist)): There's no use regretting it now.","295":"(Levin (Strategist)): The bridge over the Miletos Strait will soon be repaired. Let's advance on Chalphy.","296":"(Celice): Chalphy... father's homeland...","297":"(Levin (Strategist)): That's right, the people must surely be waiting for your return. We can't afford to dawdle in a place like this.","298":"(Celice): You're right. Let's go, to Chalphy!","299":"(Arvis): Bishop Palmarch, take the children and flee this castle.","300":"(Palmarch (elder)): Eh!? You're letting us escape?","301":"(Arvis): Mm, Julius's men will be arriving from Belhalla before long. Once that happens, it'll be too late — hurry, flee.","302":"(Palmarch (elder)): Y-, yes sir! Thank you, Your Majesty Arvis.","303":"(Arvis): And one more thing — I'll leave this in your care.","304":"(Palmarch (elder)): Th-, this is...","305":"(Arvis): You were once one of Sigurd's close aides, weren't you. Then you should understand what this means.","306":"(Palmarch (elder)): Y-, yes sir...","307":"(Arvis): Then go. I'm counting on you for the children!","308":"(Julia): Father.........","309":"(Arvis): Julia, I've done you a terrible wrong. You must hate me... please, forgive me.","310":"(Julia): No, not at all! I have never once, not even a single time, hated you, father.","311":"(Julia): You are such a kind man, father!","312":"(Arvis): I was a fool. I never even realized I was being used by Manfroy...","313":"(Arvis): And by the time I noticed, it had already spiraled beyond my control.","314":"(Arvis): Julius is the reincarnation of the dark god Loptous.","315":"(Arvis): He killed my beloved wife... ...and then came after you too...","316":"(Julia): At that time, mother used her very last strength, a warp spell, to let me escape.","317":"(Julia): I lost my memory from the shock of it, and after that, Levin saved me...","318":"(Julia): But mother was... killed by brother Julius... even now, it's still painful to remember...","319":"(Arvis): Julia, there's so much I want to talk to you about, but there's no time left.","320":"(Arvis): You should flee together with Bishop Palmarch too. It's dangerous to stay here.","321":"(Manfroy): That won't do at all. Lady Julia will be coming with me, to Veltomer.","322":"(Manfroy): If His Majesty the Emperor defies Prince Julius's command, then Lady Julia will have to die.","323":"(Arvis): Wh-, what did you say! Are you saying you'll take Julia hostage!? Just who do you think I am!","324":"(Manfroy): Hehehe, how much longer do you intend to think of yourself as emperor?","325":"(Manfroy): You are nothing more than a servant of Lord Julius now.","326":"(Manfroy): If you don't wish to suffer any further, be silent and obey Lord Julius's orders.","327":"(Manfroy): And those children you let escape — they too shall all die. Fohohoho...","328":"(Julia): Father!!","329":"(Arvis): Julia... ...I no longer have the power to protect you... so... take this circlet.","330":"(Arvis): This is your mother's keepsake, and... the very last thing that can protect you...","331":"(Manfroy): What are you dawdling about for!? Now, come quickly!!","332":"(Julia): Ahh, father.........","333":"(Palmarch (elder)): Qu-, quickly, run!","334":"(Girl): But Bishop, we can't go any further than this!","335":"(Boy): The dark priests are chasing us, aren't they — are we going to die!?","336":"(Palmarch (elder)): It'll be alright. Lord Celice will surely save us. Believe in the holy warrior!","337":"(Celice): Bishop, are you injured anywhere?","338":"(Palmarch (elder)): Oh, if it isn't Lord Celice! I've been waiting for you.","339":"(Palmarch (elder)): I kept pushing myself, telling myself I had to hold on until I could deliver this to you. Now, please, accept it.","340":"(Celice): Th-, this is!?","341":"(Palmarch (elder)): Chalphy's family treasure, the holy sword Tyrfing.","342":"(Celice): But, how did it come to be in your hands...","343":"(Palmarch (elder)): There are various reasons for that, but because of a promise I made to someone, I cannot say...","344":"(Celice): I see... understood. But still, I'm grateful.","345":"(Celice): So this is Tyrfing... I can truly feel power welling up within me...","346":"(Palmarch (elder)): Lord Celice, please, reclaim Chalphy Castle as soon as possible.","347":"(Palmarch (elder)): The people of the town have long been eagerly awaiting the day the prince would return.","348":"(Celice): Yes, with this holy sword, there's nothing left to fear. Please, rest assured, Bishop!","349":"(Coirpre): Lady Altena, are you injured anywhere?","350":"(Altena): Oh, Coirpre. Thank you, I'm fine.","351":"(Altena): You're the one who should be careful. Don't push yourself too hard.","352":"(Coirpre): Um... Lady Altena.","353":"(Altena): Eh, what is it?","354":"(Coirpre): I... I want to cast Magic Shield on you, Lady Altena.","355":"(Altena): My magic defense is low, so you're worried about me, is that it?","356":"(Altena): But that spell is dangerous, isn't it. It's alright, Coirpre.","357":"(Altena): I'm happy you'd think of me, but I don't want to put you in any danger.","358":"(Coirpre): Lady Altena, you doted on me, even though I had no mother of my own.","359":"(Coirpre): Please! Let me help you with something too!!","360":"(Altena): Coirpre... understood. I'll gratefully accept your feelings.","361":"(Altena): But promise me, you must never push yourself too hard. Can you swear to keep that promise?","362":"(Coirpre): Yes! I promise. I'll never push myself too hard!","363":"(Altena): Alright then, please go ahead. I'm counting on you, Coirpre.","364":"(Coirpre): Yes, understood.","365":"(Coirpre): ...oh great god Bragi... grant this one the mighty power of the gods...","366":"(Arvis): Heh, you poor, pitiable creatures — be scorched by the flames of my hell!","367":"(Arvis): ...Deirdre... Julia...","368":"(Levin (Strategist)): Celice, well done. Look, see for yourself.","369":"(Levin (Strategist)): The citizens have come out in great numbers to celebrate your return. Everyone looks truly happy.","370":"(Celice): Yeah, that's right... so this is my homeland. It gives me such a warm feeling.","371":"(Celice): But I still can't celebrate with my whole heart...","372":"(Levin (Strategist)): You're worried about Julia, aren't you. Celice, do you have feelings for her?","373":"(Celice): It's not like that, but...","374":"(Levin (Strategist)): According to the townspeople, she was taken away by Bishop Manfroy.","375":"(Levin (Strategist)): She was probably carried off somewhere in Grannvale.","376":"(Celice): Levin, Emperor Arvis has fallen, and I was able to avenge my father's grudge, but somehow, I feel empty inside.","377":"(Levin (Strategist)): That's because this battle still isn't over.","378":"(Levin (Strategist)): If anything, the real battle is only just beginning.","379":"(Levin (Strategist)): And when this holy war finally ends, you will, for the first time, come to know the whole truth.","380":"(Auntie): Ah, holy warrior! Please, save our children!!","381":"(Auntie): Our children are going to be... sacrificed to the dark god!","382":"(Villager (man)): Queen Hilda of Kronos is a terrifying woman.","383":"(Villager (man)): Joining hands with the dark priests, she forcibly takes away children, and kills wailing mothers without a second thought.","384":"(Villager (man)): That woman isn't human — she's like a devil incarnate...","385":"(Elder): Long ago, the war between the Loptr Empire and the Twelve Crusaders raged on for fifteen long years,","386":"(Elder): engulfing this entire continent in its wake.","387":"(Elder): And in the end, the saint Heim struck down Emperor Gale XVII, the dark god's avatar, and at long last, the light returned.","388":"(Elder): But... the dark god has been resurrected once again. Holy warrior, please, protect us...","389":"(Villager (man)): It's only recently that the sacrificial rituals began.","390":"(Villager (man)): Up until then, I'd heard Emperor Arvis would never permit such a thing — I wonder what on earth happened to him.","391":"(Villager (man)): Please, I beg you — take this Magic Ring, and save the children!","392":"(Villager (woman)): Prince Julius is a terrifying man.","393":"(Villager (woman)): When you look into those eyes of his, it's as if you're being drawn in, and you lose yourself completely.","394":"(Villager (woman)): I have many friends who adored Lord Julius and went to Belhalla, but every one of them has gone missing...","395":"(Elder): Defeating Prince Julius is something absolutely impossible for the likes of you, as you are now.","396":"(Elder): It's a pity, but sometimes, sacrifice is simply necessary...","397":"— Celice... Celice.........","398":"(Celice): W-, who's there? Who's calling my name?","399":"(Celice): ...Celice... ...how you've grown... co-, could it be, mother!? Is that you, mother?","400":"(Deirdre (ghost)): ...you've grown into such a fine young man... I must thank Lord Levin...........","401":"(Deirdre (ghost)): ...Celice, treasure your companions, your friends... ...never forget your gratitude toward them...........","402":"(Celice): ...y-, yes... mother! I have finally struck down Emperor Arvis! I have avenged father's grudge!","403":"(Deirdre (ghost)): I see.........then, what of Julius and Julia...........","404":"(Celice): Julius and Julia!? Mother, how is it that you know of the two of them?","405":"(Deirdre (ghost)): .........","406":"(Celice): Mother...?","407":"(Sigurd (ghost)): Celice.","408":"(Celice): Who are you? ...don't tell me... father!?","409":"(Sigurd (ghost)): Celice, you must not grow conceited. Arvis did not fall by your strength alone...","410":"(Celice): Eh, father... what do you mean by that!?","411":"(Sigurd (ghost)): Celice, know the sorrow of others. The truth is never just one single thing.","412":"(Sigurd (ghost)): If you fail to understand that, this battle will have been meaningless...","413":"(Celice): F-, father! Please, wait!","414":"(Sigurd (ghost)): ...take care of yourself.........","415":"(Celice): Mother..."};
